-     * ClientHello is a TLS Alert instead of a ServerHello, it still
-     * thinks the previous session is alive — typically because the
-     * previous Linux process exited without sending close_notify.
-     * Send a plaintext close_notify (7 bytes, no keys needed — RFC 5246
-     * §7.2.1 allows this since we don't have keys yet) to make the
-     * sensor drop its session state, then retry the handshake once. */
-    if (hr == VERIMARK_HANDSHAKE_ERR_SERVER_ALERT) {
